<p style="margin-left: ;">Can a mixture of 1.5 mol CH<sub>3</sub>, 3 mol O<sub>2</sub>, 2 mol CO<sub>2</sub>, and 0.5 mol H<sub>2</sub>O be maintained in a 5 L flask (K<sub>c</sub> = 175)? Explain.</p>

<p style="margin-left: 40px;">-No. Q &lt; K, so the reaction will shift to the right.</p>

</div><div mt-section-origin="Bookshelves/General_Chemistry/Exercises:_General_Chemistry/Exercises:_Petrucci_et_al./14.E:_Principles_of_Chemical_Equilibria_(Exercises)" class="mt-section" id="section_124"><span id="30_2"></span><h3 style="margin-left: ;" class="editable">30</h3>

<p style="margin-left: ;">Is the following reaction in an 8 L flask at 273 K at equilibrium? Explain.</p>

